concept:competition-and-consumer-legislation-amendment-act-2011-sch-2-sec-12cb a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "12CB Unconscionable conduct in connection with financial services"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-12cb ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person must not, in trade or commerce, in connection with:  (a) the supply or possible supply of financial services to a person (other than a listed public company); or  (b) the acquisition or possible acquisition of financial services from a person (other than a listed public company); engage in conduct that is, in all the circumstances, unconscionable.  (2) This section does not apply to conduct that is engaged in only because the person engaging in the conduct:  (a) institutes legal proceedings in relation to the supply or possible supply, or in relation to the acquisition or possible acquisition; or  (b) refers to arbitration a dispute or claim in relation to the supply or possible supply, or in relation to the acquisition or possible acquisition.  (3) For the purpose of determining whether a person has contravened subsection (1):  (a) the court must not have regard to any circumstances that were not reasonably foreseeable at the time of the alleged contravention; and  (b) the court may have regard to conduct engaged in, or circumstances existing, before the commencement of this section.  (4) It is the intention of the Parliament that:  (a) this section is not limited by the unwritten law of the States and Territories relating to unconscionable conduct; and  (b) this section is capable of applying to a system of conduct or pattern of behaviour, whether or not a particular individual is ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00184  Schedule 2  Unconscionable conduct  identified as having been disadvantaged by the conduct or behaviour; and  (c) in considering whether conduct to which a contract relates is unconscionable, a court’s consideration of the contract may include consideration of:  (i) the terms of the contract; and  (ii) the manner in which and the extent to which the contract is carried out;  and is not limited to consideration of the circumstances relating to formation of the contract.  (5) In this section: listed public company has the same meaning as it has in the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person must not, in trade or commerce, in connection with:  (a) the supply or possible supply of financial services to a person (other than a listed public company); or  (b) the acquisition or possible acquisition of financial services from a person (other than a listed public company); engage in conduct that is, in all the circumstances, unconscionable.  (2) This section does not apply to conduct that is engaged in only because the person engaging in the conduct:  (a) institutes legal proceedings in relation to the supply or possible supply, or in relation to the acquisition or possible acquisition; or  (b) refers to arbitration a dispute or claim in relation to the supply or possible supply, or in relation to the acquisition or possible acquisition.  (3) For the purpose of determining whether a person has contravened subsection (1):  (a) the court must not have regard to any circumstances that were not reasonably foreseeable at the time of the alleged contravention; and  (b) the court may have regard to conduct engaged in, or circumstances existing, before the commencement of this section.  (4) It is the intention of the Parliament that:  (a) this section is not limited by the unwritten law of the States and Territories relating to unconscionable conduct; and  (b) this section is capable of applying to a system of conduct or pattern of behaviour, whether or not a particular individual is ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00184  Schedule 2  Unconscionable conduct  identified as having been disadvantaged by the conduct or behaviour; and  (c) in considering whether conduct to which a contract relates is unconscionable, a court’s consideration of the contract may include consideration of:  (i) the terms of the contract; and  (ii) the manner in which and the extent to which the contract is carried out;  and is not limited to consideration of the circumstances relating to formation of the contract.  (5) In this section: listed public company has the same meaning as i"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3be4a8eb96e154fbf6a3d139ad922570b4878d2d7c624f1874ade8f6e095ac5c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "9"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-legislation-amendment-act-2011-sch-2-sec-12cb-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-legislation-amendment-act-2011-sch-2-sec-12cb-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-legislation-amendment-act-2011-sch-2-sec-12cb-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-legislation-amendment-act-2011-sch-2-sec-12cb-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:competition-and-consumer-legislation-amendment-act-2011-sch-2-sec-12cb-ss-5 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
